//! `base.powf(k / 11)` for the Advanced sliders' twelve steps, the same on
//! every platform. The preset mapping (`advanced_preset`) raises a handful of
//! constants to a slider step; natively that is the Windows C runtime's pow,
//! and in the browser build Rust's own pow, which differed in the last bit for
//! 13 of these 144 values (September 23, 2026) and moved every coordinate of
//! a photograph traced there by up to 0.01 px. The browser build reads the
//! Windows results from this table; native builds call pow as always, and a
//! Windows test holds the table to it. Generated by work/web/gen_step_pow.py.

